##  Moderate profitability due to higher operating expenses

 &lt;!-- PHYSICAL\_PAGE\_3 --&gt;

 Given the nascent stage of GCL ' s business operations and competitive landscape owing to competition from banks and other prime housing finance companies pressuring the portfolio yields and higher operating expenses, GCL's profitability continues to remain moderate. On a consolidated basis, in FY25, GCL reported profit after tax (PAT) of ₹152 crore on total income of ₹1620 crore compared to a profit of ₹50 crore on total income of ₹889 crore in FY24. Supported by increase in net income margin (NIM; %) and decrease in operating expense (%), the ROTA (%) stood moderate at 1.07% in FY25 against 0.59% in FY24. Going forward, the company's ability to scale up business operations, while maintaining asset quality and profitability would be a key rating monitorable.

